okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Research how Codex thread goals and Claude Code /goal actually work, to give the agent (LLM) an interface to create / complete / pause / clear goals the way compact_session lets it compact itself."
reported: "User, 2026-10-07: '코덱스의 경우 목표 처리 기능이있는데 llm이 자동으로 할수없는경우많아서 llm 할수있도록 인터페이스를 지원해야한다 (compact처럼) • 목표 생성 • 완료 처리 • 일시정지 • 임의 해제 ... claude에서도 목표 설정과 유사한기능 조사하고 구현', '코덱스의 오픈소스에서 실제 동작방식을 확인할것'."
codex_source:
  read: "openai/codex tag rust-v0.160.1, commit d27764b82f7118f674371e6d6e76271d9d606edb (sparse clone codex-rs/). Not diffed against 0.159.x / 0.160.0 (fleet runs 0.160.0/0.160.1; Ara 0.159.3 earlier)."
  feature: "features.goals, Stage::Stable, default_enabled true (features/src/lib.rs:1702-1707). Config [goals] max_goal_token_budget."
  model_tools: "ext/goal/src/spec.rs + tool.rs: get_goal; create_goal{objective, token_budget?} (only when no goal or the goal is complete; status active); update_goal{status} limited to complete|blocked|paused (tool.rs:248-256: resume, budget/usage-limited are user/system controlled). The model cannot resume or clear."
  app_server: "app-server-protocol/src/protocol/common.rs:608-622: thread/goal/set {threadId, objective?, status?, tokenBudget?} (status active|paused|blocked|usageLimited|budgetLimited|complete; creates when absent), thread/goal/get, thread/goal/clear (deletes the row); notifications thread/goal/updated, thread/goal/cleared (common.rs:1929-1930)."
  tui: "GOAL_USAGE 'Usage: /goal [<objective>|clear|edit|pause|resume]' (tui/src/goal_display.rs:5); pause -> Paused, resume -> Active (chatwidget/slash_dispatch.rs); /goal <text> asks for confirmation before replacing a goal that is not complete (per research agent: app/thread_goal_actions.rs:132-231). No 'complete' subcommand. The TUI interrupt (Esc/Ctrl+C) pauses the goal client-side (per research agent: chatwidget/interaction.rs:645-656)."
  continuation: "ext/goal/src/runtime.rs continue_if_idle (:425-): when the thread goes idle and the goal is Active (no deferral row, tools available) the runtime starts a turn with the <codex_internal_context source=\"goal\"> continuation template, turn_trigger 'goal'."
  blocked_by_system: "Per research agent (extension.rs:397-421, runtime.rs:302-331, accounting.rs): a turn error, 3 consecutive empty automatic turns, or 3 turns with failed exec and no successful tool set Blocked; budget exhaustion sets budgetLimited; usage limit sets usageLimited. Not individually re-verified."
  external_control: "Per research agent: no ownership check on thread/goal/*; live effects (immediate continuation) need the app-server process that owns the thread (GoalService runtime registry); a plain TUI has no non-interactive way except typing /goal. Not tested at runtime."
claude_docs:
  source: "https://code.claude.com/docs/en/goal.md (fetched 2026-10-07)."
  command: "/goal <condition> (up to 4,000 chars; replaces an active goal; starts a turn immediately), /goal (status), /goal clear (aliases stop, off, reset, none, cancel). One goal per session; restored on --continue/--resume; works with -p."
  mechanism: "A session-scoped prompt-based Stop hook: after each turn the small fast model returns not-yet-met (keep going), met (clear, achieved), or impossible (clear, failed). Stops without progress after several no-tool turns; clears on errors the user must fix; retries or pauses on other errors (v2.1.269+). CLAUDE_CODE_GOAL_CHECKIN_MINUTES controls check-ins/retries. No pause/resume subcommand. Unavailable when hooks are disabled or allowManagedHooksOnly."
observed_in_fleet: "Celly 2026-10-06 04:45:50Z: the model called update_goal({status:'blocked'}) itself; afterwards no continuation (journal 2026/10/06/diagnostics/codex-routed/turn-stop-goal-continuation.okf). Kobe never had a goal."
status: "research only. Implementation plan (MCP tool session_goal: set/get/complete/pause/resume/clear via thread/goal/* for app-server sessions, typed /goal for the Codex TUI and Claude Code) put on hold by the user 2026-10-07 ('아니보류'). Nothing implemented."
